  1920x1080    2039px  1.9 scr    3194px  3.0 scr   +1155
  1440x900     2354px  2.6 scr    3373px  3.7 scr   +1019
  390x844      5507px  6.5 scr    8920px 10.6 scr   +3413

AND THE READING THAT CHANGES WHAT THAT MEANS - cuts OPEN, 1920:
  before 8682px, after 8057px. The TOTAL content shrank by 625px. So
  nothing was added; the estate came out from under a cut, which is
  what ADR-0054 D5 asked for. What grew is the default view.

  the 390px overflow - 169.13px, #history > table - is present in the
  BEFORE column at the same size. Pre-existing, and now checked rather
  than assumed.

  two broken words are NEW and are in this phase's own contour:
    read-only                            #suites .node .asserts  @1920
    tests/playwright/tests/regression    #suites .node .head .name @1440
  the second is a path in the field that holds a NAME, which is why
  `.node .head .name` sets overflow-wrap: break-word and why the gate
  calls a break there a defect. Fixed below. The first is prose with a
  hyphen and is left to the next measurement to say whether it survives
  the reflow - guessing at it would be the thing this file is against.

=== AFTER THE COMPACTION, SAME INSTRUMENT ============================
  viewport     before(6d0ee53)  drawn     compacted   vs before
  2560x1440    2039px           3194px    3116px      +1077
  1920x1080    2039px  1.9scr   3194px    3116px  2.9 +1077
  1440x900     2354px           3373px    3266px      + 912
  390x844      5507px           8920px    8579px      +3072
  cuts OPEN, 1920: 8682 before, 7979 after. Total content is 703px
