THE COMPACTION BOUGHT 78px, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE STORY OF IT.
One row of environment tag across four estate rows. The touched-by line
was two lines only on `rds`, and a grid row is as tall as its tallest
card, so shortening the others changed nothing. Estate height is rows x
card height, the rows come from the 18.5rem step, and that step is 20j's
measured "a name does not wrap" figure - 295.58px, re-measured here and
unchanged. There are no cheap hundreds of pixels in it.

  the packing, at 1920, at-rest: map 813.75px in 4 columns, air 1304.6px
    map row 450.30px  Build 201.18 / Apply-stage 123.24 (0 nodes) /
                      Provision 201.18 / Quality gate 450.30 (4 nodes)
    map row 353.86px  Approve 170.80 / Apply-prod 123.24 (0 nodes) /
                      Quality gate 288.24 / Destroy 353.87
    the floor: every word whole 143.69px ("environment"),
               every name unwrapped 295.58px

BROKEN WORDS, AFTER: the path is gone from the name field at 1440. One
new entry survives - `read-only` in #suites .asserts at 1920 - and it is
a FALSE POSITIVE of a rule with no concept of a hyphen: the rule exempts
fields marked `overflow-wrap: anywhere`, which are identifiers, and this
is prose breaking at its own hyphen. measure-page is a report, not a
gate; it is not in assets/gates.json and this reddens nothing. Recorded
rather than fixed, because mangling the data with U+2011 to quiet a
report line is the worse trade.

